(project pricklypear-notes
 (doc "Pricklypear book chapter: notes — outline-first personal knowledge (org-roam / org-mode / Obsidian-shaped) as Nopales on the one-tree substrate")
 (status partial)
 (* agent note (|2026-08-02 status reconcile: core notes surface is live (doc/get, /notes, search, wiki, roam). Remaining partial: outline-actions (op-protocol refile + full structed set), garden-import (pass-2 uuid edges), tree-cutover finish slices.|) *)
 (convention ocaml-dune)
 (section notes
  (doc "Outline-first notes OS: tree documents, wiki links, dailies, capture, hypermedia structure edit, garden import")
  (status partial)
  
  (verify
   (build "dune build image")
   (smoke "(load-library \"outline\") then pure tree ops on a sample node tree")
   (smoke "(load-library \"notes\") installs /notes and notes/*")
   (smoke "create note with nested outline; GET /notes?slug=… shows foldable tree")
   (smoke "[[slug]] in node body becomes link; backlinks partial lists inbound")
   (smoke "(bible Gen 2 3) in body renders dabar href; unknown book degrades")
   (smoke "(notes/daily) get-or-creates today's daily outline")
   (smoke "pp_eval '(notes/get \"…\")' returns outline value for agents")
   (smoke "tree: folder + note + heading children round-trip via notes/doc/*")
   (smoke "import dry-run of vault md reports counts without writing"))
  (details
   (doc (|
        =========================================================
        PRODUCT INTENT
        =========================================================
        Build a personal knowledge environment on the live image
        inspired by:
          - org-mode: hierarchical OUTLINES as the document model
          - org-roam: stable ids/slugs, backlinks, dailies, capture
          - Obsidian: fast browse, wiki links, folder garden

        NOT a port of Electron Obsidian or Emacs.
        NOT continuous file-backed markdown under libs/ or disk.
        Notes are durable TREE NODES in Postgres, edited live.
        One-shot vault import (Obsidian md) is in-scope; sync is not.

        WHY THIS OS:
          Every note/outline is a Nopales value. Agents and humans use
          the same functions via REPL / pp_eval / htmx. No notes REST
          API to invent — the image is the API.

        =========================================================
        PRIORITY ORDER (locked)
        =========================================================
        1. One-tree note substrate (folders, notes, heading children)
        2. Outline algebra on heading nodes (structed/outline ops)
        3. UUID wiki links + backlinks; bible sexp refs → dabar
        4. Personal garden isolation (not system/main content)
        5. Daily notes + capture / inbox
        6. Migrate existing PP notes; import Obsidian vault md
        7. Tags / search polish — RESOLVED by subsection search-modal
        8. Graph visualization (optional, late)

        =========================================================
        PACKAGES
        =========================================================
        outline/   — pure tree ADT + structure ops (no DB)
        structed/  — generic structural-edit algebra
        notes/     — persistence façade, routes, dailies, capture
        roam/      — link parse/reindex/render (UUID-backed)
        bible/ + dabar/ — reader + study; bible sexp render target

        =========================================================
        OUT OF SCOPE (v1)
        =========================================================
        - Full org-mode syntax (drawers, babel, agenda, clock)
        - Full CommonMark / markdown WYSIWYG
        - Force-directed graph as launch requirement
        - Continuous Obsidian/FS vault sync (one-shot import only)
        - TeX/PDF/video/EXPORT pipeline ingest from vault
        - Doltgres / DB engine swap for note history
        - Per-note function_defs (notes are data, not code)
        - Real-time multiplayer CRDT on one outline
        - Full per-lens versioned /data (one-tree placement B);
          garden isolation is path+author scoped (see personal-garden)
   |))
  )

  (subsection outline-model
   (doc "Sexp outline ADT: node tree with stable ids — org structure as data")
   (status verified)
   (implements libs/outline/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "outline/node constructors and outline/html produce nested details")
    (smoke "outline/promote demote move-up move-down preserve ids")
    (smoke "round-trip: print tree text then parse back (or JSON props path)"))

   (details
    (doc (|
         CANONICAL SHAPE (implementation may use lists/dicts):

           A node is a record with:
             id     — stable string (uuid or short id), required
             title  — string, required
             body   — string, optional prose (may contain [[slug]])
             todo   — "" | "TODO" | "DONE" | future keywords
             kids   — list of child nodes (order matters)

         Suggested Nopales construction helpers:

           (outline/node title) 
           (outline/node title body)
           (outline/node* props kids)   ; props = alist or dict JSON

         Tree = root node. In-memory ADT unchanged. Persistence is
         heading children under the note path (notes.storage); the
         legacy fields.outline JSON blob is retired after cutover.

         WHY SEXPS:
           Nested lists ARE outlines. No heading-level parser.
           pp_expr / pretty printers already exist for readability.
           Structure edit = pure functions on values.

         PATHS:
           Prefer id-based addressing over index paths so reorder
           does not break ops:
             (outline/find tree id) -> node | nil
             (outline/update tree id f) -> tree
             (outline/insert-child tree parent-id new-node) -> tree
             (outline/delete tree id) -> tree
             (outline/promote tree id) / demote / move-up / move-down

         FOLD STATE:
           v1: browser <details> open attribute only (ephemeral).
           Optional later: collapsed-ids set in note props or session.

         PRINT/PARSE:
           In-memory: list/ADT via outline/* constructors.
           On disk after cutover: one heading tree_node per outline
           node (notes.storage). encode/decode helpers still exist
           for import, tests, and whole-subtree replace serialization.

         PURE PACKAGE:
           libs/outline/lib.pp must not touch storage so it can
           be unit-tested / reused by other apps (e.g. project plans).
    |))
   )
  )

  (subsection storage
   (doc "Notes as one-tree nodes: folders, note leaves, heading children; notes/* façade")
   (status implemented)
   (* agent note (|2026-08-02: notes/doc/* façade on tree (libs/notes/doc + lib.pp); live (notes/doc/get "agents") returns uuid/slug/title/outline; tree/garden-root path grammar in tree_store.ml.|) *)
   (implements libs/notes/lib.pp libs/notes/capture/lib.pp libs/notes/migrate/lib.pp libs/notes/tree/lib.pp image/lib/tree_store.ml image/lib/crud.ml)
   (verify
    (smoke "notes/upsert then notes/get by slug returns outline")
    (smoke "second upsert same slug updates in place (idempotent)")
    (smoke "folder path nesting depth > 1 via tree list")
    (smoke "outline headings persist as heading children under note path")
    (smoke "rename/move note keeps uuid; links still resolve")
    (build "dune build image"))

   (details
    (doc (|
         =========================================================
         ONE-TREE NOTES (replaces flat data_rows note blob)
         =========================================================
         Flat CRUD (get/create/update/rows on type note) remains for
         other product types. Notes leave that path. See also the
         index-read-path subsection for how every read (index +
         detail) resolves to the one tree store and how the legacy
         rows fallback is retired.

         PATH GRAMMAR (hierarchical; not data.<type>.<uuid>):
           data.note.u.<user>.…                 — user garden root
           data.note.u.<user>.<folder>…         — folder (kind=folder)
           data.note.u.<user>.….<slug>          — note leaf (kind=note)
           data.note.u.<user>.….<slug>.h.<nid>  — outline heading
                                                   (kind=heading)

         Readable slug labels: [a-z0-9-]+ only (ltree-safe). Type
         name segment stays literal "note" (not enc_label base64).

         KINDS (tree_nodes.kind; reverse-mirror ignores these — they
         must NEVER be written as kind=datum or path segment-3 will
         be misread as a uuid by tree_from_nodes):
           folder   payload body: {uuid, title}
           note     payload body: {uuid, slug, title, tags, kind, day,
                                   source_id?, source_path?}
                    NO outline blob — children are truth
           heading  payload body: {id, title, body, todo}
                    kids = real child heading nodes under path

         IDENTITY:
           uuid  — stable; wiki links and refile target this
           slug  — last path label of the note; globally unique
                   per user garden (enforce on upsert)
           title — display only; independent of slug

         OUTLINE LOAD/SAVE:
           In-memory ADT stays outline/* + structed/* (id title body
           todo kids). Load rebuilds ADT from heading subtree.
           Save v1 may whole-replace heading children under note.h
           in one transaction; fine-grained op→tree/move is a
           tighten pass, not a blocker.

         FAÇADE (preserve call shapes where possible):
           notes/doc/get|upsert|list|set-folder|… keep agent/UI ABI.
           Internals call tree prims, not (create 'note …).

         KERNEL PRIMS (tree_store + thin register; additive):
           (tree/get path)
           (tree/list prefix [depth])
           (tree/upsert path kind type body-json)
           (tree/delete path [recursive?])
           (tree/move old-path new-path)   — subtree path rewrite
           (tree/find-by type field value)
           (tree/get-uuid uuid)
         Flat get/create/update/rows ABI unchanged for todos/etc.

         NOTE-LINK: see links-and-roam (UUID edges).

         NOT IN function_defs / system/main seed:
           Note *content* is never package defaults. pp_sync does
           not pull garden notes. notes/* outline/* roam/* CODE may
           promote to main; content stays in the user garden path.

         LEGACY:
           Existing data_rows type=note rows migrate once (M0) into
           tree nodes; after cutover notes/* does not write them.
           folder string field and JSON outline field are retired.
           M0 must EXPLODE each outline blob into real heading child
           nodes under the note path (no inline outline blob), and
           normalize path labels to the kebab slug. After every uuid
           verifies in the tree, the legacy data_rows type=note rows
           are DELETED (no permanent inert archive).

         HISTORY: v1 overwrite on save (updated_at). No Doltgres.
    |))
   )
  )

  (subsection links-and-roam
   (doc "Wiki links [[slug]] as UUID edges; bible sexps → dabar; media embeds")
   (status implemented)
   (* agent note (|2026-08-02: libs/roam (parse-links via extract-links prim, reindex note-link from_uuid/to_uuid, backlinks, render-body/media); live roam/backlinks on agents. Refile still ad-hoc package not op-protocol — tracked under outline-actions.|) *)
   (verify
    (smoke "body with [[other]] creates note-link UUID edge on save")
    (smoke "(roam/backlinks slug) lists inbound links after resolve")
    (smoke "render turns [[other]] into anchor using current slug/title")
    (smoke "move/rename note does not require reindex; links still resolve")
    (smoke "refile/extract of a node does not require roam/reindex (uuid stable)")
    (smoke "[[media:uuid|alt]] renders img; not indexed as note-link")
    (smoke "(bible Gen 2 3) renders /dabar href; (bible …) not a note-link")
    (smoke "Obsidian [[bible:Genesis2:3|…]] import normalizes to bible sexp")
    (smoke "(extract-links body) matches roam/parse-links edge cases")
    (test "image primitives_test extract-links cases"))
   (implements
    libs/roam/lib.pp
    libs/notes/lib.pp
    libs/notes/refile/lib.pp
    libs/bible/lib.pp
    libs/dabar/lib.pp
    image/lib/prims_pure.ml)
   (details
    (doc (|
         =========================================================
         NOTE-LINK = UUID EDGE (not slug pair as source of truth)
         =========================================================
         TYPE note-link (data row or tree datum — implementation
         choice; shape is what matters):
           from_uuid  — source note uuid (stable)
           from_id    — source heading id ("" = whole-note)
           to_uuid    — target note uuid (stable)
           to_id      — target heading id optional
           label      — optional display label
           kind       — "wikilink" | future
         Optional cached from_slug/to_slug for debug only — never
         authoritative. Index by (from_uuid, to_uuid).
         Live package: libs/roam (parse-links, reindex, backlinks,
         render-body, backlinks-html).

         AUTHORING SYNTAX (bodies, still human-friendly):
           [[slug]]              — wiki by slug at write time
           [[slug|label]]        — labeled wiki
           [[media:uuid|alt]]    — media embed (not note-link)
           (bible BOOK ch [verse]) — sexp bible ref (not note-link)
           (bible BOOK ch verse-from verse-to) — optional range
         BOOK accepts full name or bible abbrev (Gen, John, …);
         normalized via bible/abbrev-of + bible/parse-ref helpers.
         No #node-id deep links v1.

         SAVE-TIME RESOLUTION:
           [[slug]] -> lookup note uuid (tree/find-by / notes/doc);
           store edge uuid→uuid. Missing target: stub-link without
           edge until target exists (prefer). Bible sexps are NOT
           note-link rows.

         REINDEX:
           (roam/reindex note-uuid outline-tree) replaces edges for
           from_uuid. Called on content-touching saves only
           (set-body, upsert with body change, op=eval target=body).
           Move/rename/refile/extract does NOT reindex — note and
           heading uuids/ids stay stable; edges remain valid. Cached
           from_slug/to_slug may go stale; resolve via uuid at read.

         =========================================================
         REFILE / EXTRACT vs LINKS (align tree-browser + op-protocol)
         =========================================================
         Refile and extract are STRUCTURAL moves of outline subtrees
         across note documents — they are NOT link-graph operations.
         Today: libs/notes/refile (ad-hoc dual upsert). Target:
           structural-editing.op-protocol owns the wire
             POST {op, target, args} → fragment + OOB selection
           named ops e.g. refile / extract-note with args
             (dst-slug) or (new-slug?) — server applies pure tree
             surgery then whole-doc write via notes/doc/*.
         image.tree-browser deliberately defers refile/move UI
         until those ops exist on the shared protocol (no parallel
         /tree/refile routes). notes.outline-actions already lists
         this gap. When protocol lands:
           - notes/refile and notes/refile/extract become thin
             adapters or disappear into op dispatch
           - roam edges need no rewrite (uuid stable)
           - tree-browser may offer move only via the same ops

         RENDER:
           Wiki: resolve to_uuid → current slug/title/path; anchor
           /notes?slug=<current>. Broken uuid → muted missing.
           Media: unchanged img path.
           Bible sexp: template via bible/dabar —
             (bible/link-html book ch verse [label])
               -> <a href="/dabar?book=…&chapter=…&verse=…">…</a>
             optional hx-get into #dabar-panel when chrome present.
           Kernel extract-links / render-links gain bible-sexp
           recognition (budget-safe OCaml), or Nopales pre-pass
           normalizes sexps before render-links — prefer OCaml once
           syntax is frozen.

         IMPORT NORMALIZE (garden-import):
           Obsidian [[bible:Genesis2:3|Label]] and bare
           [[bible:Hosea4:6]] become (bible Hosea 4 6) text in
           heading bodies (Label dropped or becomes visible prose
           adjacent — keep label as link text via
           (bible Hosea 4 6 "Hosea 4:6") if three-or-four arg form
           includes optional label string).

         QUERY:
           (roam/backlinks slug-or-uuid) -> inbound with current
           titles/slugs for display. UI partial: notes-backlinks.

         NOT v1:
           - graph view renderer
           - unlinked-mentions auto-discovery
           - block-ref transclusion
           - path-qualified wiki links for duplicate slugs
           - tree-browser-initiated refile (waits on op-protocol)
    |))
   )
  )

  (subsection budget-scale
   (doc "Per-call eval budget: stress contracts for notes/roam/outline so large trees and bodies never Budget_exceeded on ordinary UI/agent paths")
   (status implemented)
   (implements
    lisp/lib/eval.ml
    image/lib/prims_pure.ml
    libs/notes/lib.pp
    libs/outline/lib.pp
    libs/std/lib.pp
    scripts/verify_budget_stress.py
    scripts/verify_notes_execute_all.py)
   (verify
    (build "dune build")
    (test "dune runtest — lisp list-hof + image extract-links")
    (smoke "scripts/verify_budget_stress.py (monitor-rerunnable)")
    (smoke "parse: 500+ wiki links in one body completes; count matches")
    (smoke "reindex/upsert: 10 nodes x ~8k body with links indexes all links")
    (smoke "render: outline/html on large tree/body returns HTML, no budget error")
    (smoke "many-node ops: N structure ops each in own eval (HTTP-shaped)")
    (smoke "(budget-remaining) positive mid-call; floor asserted after stress cases"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         WHY:
           The 100k step default_limit is a safety net, not a perf
           governor. Char-scanners and recursive list walks in Nopales
           burned the budget on ordinary notes (upsert reindex,
           large inbox render) while the write sometimes committed
           first — silent stale links. Hot paths move to OCaml or
           kernel special forms; stress tests guard regressions.

         BUDGET MODEL (lisp-interpreter.eval):
           - One budget per eval/call_handler invocation
           - tick on each eval step; Budget_exceeded aborts that call
           - OCaml prims cost one tick at the call site (body free)
           - (budget-remaining) -> steps left (dynamic current budget)
           - (bench expr-string [n]) -> avg us/iter for calibration
           Do NOT "fix" scale bugs by raising default_limit.

         KERNEL / HOT PATHS (required):
           - list/map, list/filter, list/foldl: special forms
             (OCaml loop + apply); not O(n) Nopales recursion frames
           - extract-links: OCaml; roam/parse-links uses it
           - select-for-update: error outside with-transaction
             (reliability adjacent to long evals)
           Planned if stress fails render/tree:
             OCaml render-links (or roam/render-body prim)
             cheaper outline encode/decode/find if tree ops dominate

         STRESS SUITE (scripts/verify_budget_stress.py):
           Monitor-rerunnable against a running image (dev or
           habitat) via pp_eval. Synthetic fixtures only — do not
           mutate user garden notes without a dedicated test slug
           prefix (e.g. budget-stress-*) cleaned up after.

           Suites:
           1. PARSE / EXTRACT
              - correctness edges (3 links, 0, unclosed, [[]], media)
              - scale: single body with >=500 links completes
              - optional: 10k-char link-free body still cheap
           2. REINDEX / UPSERT
              - tree: >=10 nodes, each body >=8k with >=1 link
              - notes/doc/upsert returns ok (not budget exceeded)
              - note-link count for slug == expected wiki links
              - budget-remaining floor after call (implementation
                picks a conservative floor; document in script)
           3. RENDER
              - outline/html (or show-body without request deps) on
                large tree: many nodes and/or one ~32k+ body
              - must return non-empty HTML string; no budget error
              - wiki + media syntax appear as anchors/img when hook
                is roam/render-body
           4. MANY-NODE ACTIONS
              - create synthetic note with >=50 child nodes
              - each op in its own eval (mirrors HTTP call_handler):
                cycle-todo, move-up/down, archive, set-title
              - extract one node to its own note; refile one node
              - every op ok; final tree consistent; cleanup slugs
           5. THRESHOLD PIN (optional / nightly)
              - binary-search max body size for parse vs render
              - log or store result; not a hard CI flake gate unless
                threshold collapses below known-good baseline

         ACCEPTANCE:
           verify_budget_stress.py exits 0 on local dev.sh image
           and on habitat after deploy. verify_notes_execute_all.py
           remains the broader feature smoke; budget script owns
           scale. Failures file as product bugs (reindex/render),
           not "raise the limit".

         OUT OF SCOPE HERE:
           - Jane Street Incremental / BI pipelines
           - raising default_limit as the primary fix
           - preemptive multi-request chunking of a single note view
    |))
   )
  )

  (subsection outline-actions
   (doc "Per-node outline action menu; the eval op turns nodes into a live Nopales surface")
   (status partial)
   (* agent note (|2026-08-02 confirm still partial: notes/outline/apply-op + eval + POST /partials/notes-node-op shipped; notes/refile* exist but not on structural-editing.op-protocol; full structed wrap/splice/raise not all on outline menu.|) *)
   (implements
    libs/notes/outline/lib.pp
    libs/notes/refile/lib.pp
    libs/outline/lib.pp
    libs/structed/lib.pp
    libs/notes/lib.pp
    image/lib/http.ml)
   (verify
    (smoke "structure ops: add-child/sibling delete move promote/demote archive cycle-todo set-title/body")
    (smoke "slurp-forward / barf-forward via structed/* on outline accessors")
    (smoke "op=eval target=child splices returned string as a new child node")
    (smoke "op=eval target=sibling splices; target=body replaces this node body")
    (smoke "eval expr binds self/doc/slug to current context")
    (smoke "eval reindexes roam links when a body changes")
    (smoke "refile: node moves to another note root kids")
    (smoke "extract: node becomes its own note; removed from source")
    (smoke "POST /partials/notes-node-op returns outline partial + selection")
    (smoke "scripts/verify_budget_stress.py many-node actions suite"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         SHIPPED SURFACE (libs/notes/outline + outline + structed):
           notes/outline/apply-op dispatches structure ops on the
           outline tree value. Ops present today:
             add-child add-sibling delete move-up move-down
             promote demote set-title set-body set-todo
             cycle-todo archive unarchive
             slurp-forward barf-forward  (via structed/* +
               outline/kids outline/set-kids — op-protocol preview)
           Selection companion: notes/outline/apply-op-sel →
           (list tree' sel) for OOB restore.

         WIRE (reconcile — code wins over older spec path):
           POST /partials/notes-node-op
             params: slug, op, node-id [, title|body|todo|expr|target]
           NOT /partials/notes-op (stale name). Fragment path → no
           chrome (wants_fragment). Client hx-target #outline
           hx-swap outerHTML; selection via hidden OOB when present.

         op = eval
           Form: notes/outline/eval-form → same partial endpoint.
           notes/outline/eval-result loads
             (lambda (self doc slug) <expr>)
           and applies it. target in {child, sibling, body} via
           notes/outline/eval-target (default child).
           result handling by target:
             body     as-str → outline/set-body on node
             child    string → new node title; valid outline node
                      sexp → splice subtree under id
             sibling  same as child, insert after id

         REFILE / EXTRACT (libs/notes/refile — NOT yet op-protocol):
           notes/refile src-slug nid dst-slug — detach node from
           src outline, add-child under dst root, dual upsert.
           notes/refile/extract — detach → new note slug from title,
           remove from source. These are whole-doc outline writes
           via notes/doc or legacy notes/upsert. When
           structural-editing.op-protocol lands for cross-doc moves,
           refile/extract MUST become named tree-ops on that
           protocol (same POST shape, server-authoritative tree),
           not parallel ad-hoc routes. image.tree-browser defers
           refile/move UI until then.

         PERSISTENCE:
           Structure ops upsert through notes/doc/* (tree store).
           Body-touching ops should roam/reindex (verify smoke).

         WHY:
           Notes view = live Nopales surface. wiki-llm-loop is the
           first major consumer of op=eval splices.

         SECURITY:
           eval runs full session prim set incl DB — treat as REPL.
           Auth gate only boundary v1; v2 may confirm destructive
           prims.

         GAPS (keep status partial until closed):
           - full structed op set (wrap/splice/raise/…) not all
             wired into apply-op / keymap
           - refile/extract not on op-protocol wire yet
           - budget stress suite must stay green on garden-scale
    |))
   )
  )

  (subsection wiki-llm-loop
   (doc "LLM-maintained wiki over the notes corpus — ingest, query, lint as Nopales ops")
   (status implemented)
   (* agent note (|2026-08-02: libs/wiki/lib.pp — wiki/ingest-from-source, wiki/query, wiki/lint, wiki/events, wiki/schema, wiki-event rows; live wiki/schema ok.|) *)
   (implements libs/wiki/lib.pp libs/notes/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "(wiki/ingest-from-source TEXT) creates/updates a source note + entity/concept notes + note-link rows")
    (smoke "(wiki/query QUESTION) synthesizes with [[slug]] citations; may file-back a kind=query note")
    (smoke "(wiki/lint) returns orphans/contradictions/missing-pages/suggested-sources")
    (smoke "each top-level wiki op writes one wiki-event row; (wiki/events) lists them")
    (smoke "agents drive ingest/query/lint via eval (pp_eval); no /wiki/* routes require registration"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         PATTERN:
           A persistent, compounding wiki over curated sources: the
           LLM does not retrieve raw chunks per query; it reads the
           existing corpus, integrates each new source into the
           notes (page updates, cross-links, contradiction flags),
           and keeps synthesis current. The corpus IS the knowledge
           base.

         SHAPE:
           Notes ARE wiki pages; kind discriminates role. The agent
           drives operations through ordinary Nopales functions exposed
           to the REPL; the user reaches the same operations through
           the outline-actions eval op on a source node. No /wiki/*
           routes for v1 — the existing /notes surface plus the live
           eval surface cover the user-facing flow.

         BUILD ORDER (dependencies):
           1. image.per-request-context — so notes routes survive the
              cotenant race: anonymous attach flips the shared
              Session.t routes/env mid-request and any
              personal-branch route 404s under traffic until
              per-request-context lands. Deployable on system/main
              as a documented workaround in the meantime.
           2. notes.links-and-roam (note-link rows + roam/parse-links
              + roam/reindex + roam/backlinks).
           3. notes.outline-actions (the eval op for LLM splices).

         NOTE KINDS (convention over the existing note row schema;
         widening the note.kind vocabulary — no new storage):
           note       existing default (behavior preserved)
           daily      existing dailies
           source     source-summary page (per ingested raw source)
           entity     a named thing (person, place, work)
           concept    an abstract topic
           query      a filed-back synthesis with citations
           synthesis  cross-source integration/comparison
           schema     the corpus preamble note (see below)
           log        reserve; not used v1 (audit is wiki-event rows)

         DOC-LEVEL FRONTMATTER (extends the note row, NOT per-node
         metadata — avoids a node-schema migration):
           updated_at   timestamp of last ingest/query touch
           updated_by   "llm" | username | "agent"
           source_count for source/entity/concept: number of distinct
                        sources contributing; incremented on ingest

         SCHEMA-NOTE CONVENTION:
           A note with kind=schema holds prose describing this
           corpus's conventions, page disciplines, and ingest
           emphasis; co-evolved by the human and the LLM.
           (wiki/schema) returns its body string, seeded with a
           sensible default at first call. ingest/query/lint read it
           as the LLM preamble. There is no separate schema-agent
           path — it is just another note the loop reads.

         OPS (each is one top-level Nopales call; each writes one
         wiki-event row on success):
           (wiki/ingest-from-source source-text [slug-hint])
             1. create/update a source note (kind=source) carrying
                the source text + extracted summary outline.
             2. read (wiki/schema) + (roam/backlinks)/index over the
                current corpus; build the prompt.
             3. (ai/ask prompt) -> a JSON plan:
                  { summary_node, entities[], concepts[],
                    links[{from,to,kind}], followups[] }
             4. notes/upsert each entity/concept page (kind=entity |
                concept), composed with the source's contribution;
                bump source_count; stamp updated_at / updated_by.
             5. (roam/reindex) the affected slugs.
             6. write one wiki-event row (kind=ingest, op-slug, ts,
                summary).
             Return the new source-summary slug + the list of pages
             touched.

           (wiki/query question)
             read (wiki/schema) + the most relevant pages (roam /
             find-text over the corpus index); synthesize with
             [[slug]] citations. Optionally file-back as a kind=query
             note that child-references its cited pages. One
             wiki-event row (kind=query).

           (wiki/lint)
             one (ai/ask) pass over schema + index + note-link edges;
             report orphans, contradictions, stale claims, missing
             pages (concepts mentioned but lacking their own page),
             suggested new sources. Optionally draft stubs for
             missing entities (opt-in create-stubs? arg). One
             wiki-event row (kind=lint).

         AUDIT:
           TYPE wiki-event (rows; fields: kind op slug ts summary):
             append-only, branch-shared, one row per top-level wiki
             op (ingest/query/lint). NOT autonomic — only these
             three top-level ops write events. Helper calls
             (roam/backlinks, outline/eval, etc.) do not write
             events. Retention is opt-in:
               (wiki/events [since])    -> list recent events
               (wiki/prune-events days) -> drop events older than N
                                           days (explicit, manual)
             Corpus content evolution is recorded in the notes
             themselves (updated_at/by frontmatter); the wiki-event
             stream is operational audit, not content of record.

         LIVE TELEMETRY (separate stream, unchanged infra):
           ingest/query/lint emit Info/Error into the existing
           Ops_log ring (component "wiki") so a long op is visible
           via (log-tail). Bounded 5000 + rotates; not a permanent
           audit. Two streams, two purposes: Ops_log = live
           observability of this request; wiki-event rows = audit
           trail of what the wiki has done to itself.

         NOT v1 (deferred):
           - URL fetch / clipper (user pastes text first)
           - markdown (outlines ARE the substrate; no marked.js)
           - graph view renderer (note-link rows hold the structure)
           - unlinked-mentions auto-discovery
           - block-ref transclusion
           - images / attachments
           - batch / unsupervised ingest sweep
    |))
   )
  )

