  (subsection index-read-path
   (doc "Notes index reads resolve to the tree store exactly once; legacy data_rows fallback retired; interim read-layers removed")
   (status implemented)
   (implements
    libs/notes/lib.pp
    libs/notes/doc/lib.pp
    libs/notes/ui/lib.pp
    image/lib/tree_store.ml)
   (verify
    (smoke "GET /notes lists garden folders incl. tree-only notes")
    (smoke "GET /notes?folder=garden/bible/scripture_concepts lists its notes")
    (smoke "(notes/list-light) equals notes/doc/index-list (both tree)")
    (smoke "(notes/doc/get slug) and /notes?slug=… agree for tree-only slug")
    (smoke "no binding under notes/light/* remains on the image")
    (smoke "no call site of (rows 'note) outside notes/migrate/legacy-*"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         PROBLEM (drift this closes):
           The index accumulated overlapping read layers while the
           one-tree cutover was landing:
             notes/doc/*       — dual-read façade (tree first, legacy
                                 data_rows fallback)
             notes/ui/* flat   — budget-safe flat index over
                                 notes/doc/index-list (tree via OCaml
                                 tree/note-index)
             notes/tree/render — original nested folder tree; walks
                                 folders with Lisp list ops; exceeds
                                 the eval budget at garden scale
             notes/light/*     — live-only nested index reading legacy
                                 data_rows ONLY; became the routed
                                 /notes handler, so tree-only (garden)
                                 notes vanished from the UI while
                                 agents (façade) still saw them
           One /notes route pointed at whichever layer happened to be
           loaded last. Result: index and detail disagreed; garden
           invisible in UI; budget-safe code unreachable.

         TARGET — ONE READ PATH:
           Every notes read (index and detail) resolves through
           notes/doc/* to the ONE tree store exactly once:
             index  /notes           → notes/page →
                                       notes/ui/folders-html (flat,
                                       budget-safe via OCaml
                                       tree/note-index)
             detail /notes?slug=…    → notes/ui/show → notes/doc/get
             agent  notes/doc/get|list|search — unchanged (façade)
           notes/list-light is re-pointed at notes/doc/index-list so
           agent and UI see the same rows.

         SLICES:
           I1  Route /notes to notes/page (git-managed, flat index).
               Delete the live-only notes/light/* bindings; nothing
               in libs/ references them.
           I2  Retire notes/tree/render + render-folder (budget-
               unsafe at garden scale). Keep only as an explicitly
               renamed non-routed legacy binding, or delete.
           I3  notes/list-light → notes/doc/index-list (same rows,
               same order); drop its private legacy-rows read.
           I4  Retire the legacy data_rows fallback in notes/doc/*
               (list / row / find-slug). Tree is the only store.
               Precondition: M0 (migrate legacy → tree) verified for
               every legacy uuid; legacy rows kept as an inert
               archive, not read. Audit gate: no call site of
               (rows 'note) / (find-rows 'note) outside
               notes/migrate/legacy-*.

         AUDIT (I4 gate):
           Full-tree scan of libs/ + image/ confirms every note read
           outside the façade's own fallback already goes through
           notes/doc/* — no package (todo/roam/wiki/flashcards/bible/
           dabar/ai/calendar/capture/ui) reads rows 'note directly.
           Only notes/migrate/legacy-* touches legacy, by design.
           I4 is therefore a façade-internal deletion, not a
           cross-package change.

         NON-GOALS:
           - Re-raising the eval budget to save notes/tree/render
             (budget is a safety net; the nested Lisp walk is the
             bug, per budget-scale)
           - Changing the slug-page outline editor or structure ops
           - Merging/renaming garden folders for display (kebab vs
             underscore is cosmetic; path-based folders tolerate both).
             Folder GROUPING is path-derived (not the legacy folder
             string), and the garden/ import prefix strips to top
             level in the index per garden-import DISPLAY.

         CUTOVER COMPLETION (the finish line this subsection gates):
           The legacy nested index (notes/light/*) must actually be
           deleted from the image (I1) so /notes serves the flat
           budget-safe index over tree/note-index, and that index
           groups by PATH-derived folders with the garden/ prefix
           stripped to top level. Until then the UI shows only the
           legacy-folder rows and hides garden/tree-only notes.
           Legacy data_rows type=note rows are DELETED after M0
           re-migration verifies every uuid (no permanent archive).
    |))
   )
  )

