  (subsection search-modal
   (doc "Typeahead find modal: one server search feeds open-note and refile; flat grouped results down to header level")
   (status implemented)
   (* agent note (|2026-08-02: notes/search + notes/ui/search-partial; route /partials/notes-search; live GET ?q=agents → 200 grouped hits.|) *)
   (implements libs/notes/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "GET /partials/notes-search?q=… returns grouped result HTML (docs + header rows with › breadcrumbs)")
    (smoke "results arrive without enumerating the garden in Nopales (filter happens in Postgres)")
    (smoke "modal opens via keyboard shortcut; arrows navigate; Enter opens chosen row")
    (smoke "empty query and no-match queries render stable non-error markup")
    (smoke "refile entry point uses the same typeahead; choosing a row refiles the selected node")
    (smoke "node-targeted rows refile under that heading; doc rows refile at root"))
   (details
    (doc (|
         PRODUCT:
           One find-box is the "open note" interface AND the
           "refile destination" interface. Cmd/Ctrl-K opens a modal
           with a single input; typing shows results immediately.
           This subsection resolves priority-7 "search polish".

         INTERACTION MODEL (locked: flat, grouped):
           Every keystroke re-queries the server; the result list is
           ONE flat stream grouped under doc headings, header-level
           matches indented beneath their doc with a breadcrumb path:
             JOURNAL
               2026 › July 12 session
             TODO
               Projects › pricklypear
           Arrow keys move, Enter activates. NOT a two-tier
           drill-down (→/← to enter docs): slower when you already
           know the header word, and refile wants doc+node targets
           in one list anyway.

         RESULT ROW:
           (doc-slug doc-title node-id|() header-path matched-field)
           node-id () = doc-level hit (title/tags match).
           header-path = "Gran › Parent › Header" for tree cutover
           storage; pre-cutover (fields.outline JSON blob) only
           doc-level rows are emitted — header granularity ARRIVES
           WITH the tree cutover, it is not retrofitted onto the
           blob. matched-field lets the UI badge title vs body vs
           header hits.

         SEARCH STRATEGY (v1):
           Postgres substring via the EXISTING find-text prim
           (fields->>f ILIKE '%needle%', crud.ml) over title, tags,
           and the outline payload — once per field, merged +
           deduped by slug in Nopales, capped (≤20 rows). No new
           OCaml prim for v1: three find-text calls are constant
           work regardless of garden size; garden-wide Nopales
           enumeration is FORBIDDEN on this path (BORGE-1785603757:
           ~3k notes × eager enumeration blew the 100k step budget).
           Ranking v1: exact-slug first, title hits, then header,
           then body/outline. Fuzzy/typo tolerance (pg_trgm) and
           ranked FTS (tsvector, cf. dabar.search-fts) are later
           upgrades that swap the query behind the SAME partial —
           the modal does not change. Track under .borge-bugs when
           demanded by use; not spec'd here.

         NON-GOALS (v1):
           - No load-the-whole-tree-into-JS client search
           - No tsvector/trgm migration (see above)
           - No cross-type global search (notes only; a global
             launcher is a product-experience question, later)
           - No search inside archived/hidden docs unless the
             current notes/doc/list filter already shows them

         UI / HTMX SHAPE:
           Follows the details-popover precedent of
           notes/ui/refile-modal (BORGE-1785603757) — no JS
           framework, no new asset pipeline. Modal is a <details>
           (or <dialog> if focus trapping proves needed) opened by
           clicking "find" or Cmd/Ctrl-K (tiny script, same style
           as the existing outline keyboard-nav script). Input has
             hx-get="/partials/notes-search"
             hx-trigger="input changed delay:200ms"
             hx-target on the results container.
           Arrow/Enter handling extends that script; htmx
           `htmx:afterSwap` re-focuses the first result.

         ROUTES (all private, current branch):
           GET /partials/notes-search?q=…         → grouped result HTML
           GET /partials/notes-search?q=…&mode=refile
             → same list, rows refile the selected outline node
               (POST action=refile with dst_slug + optional
                dst_node_id) instead of navigating.
           Open-note activation navigates to /notes?slug=…
           (&node=… for header rows when the tree cutover lands).

         REFILE CONVERGENCE:
           notes/ui/refile-modal's raw dst_slug text input gains a
           mode=refile typeahead against the same partial (exact
           slug entry keeps working — no regression for agents /
           keyboard-only users who know the slug). Refile to a
           header target parents the subtree under that node;
           refile to a doc row parents at root (current behavior).
           The existing POST /notes action=refile handler accepts
           an optional dst_node_id.

         BUDGET INVARIANT:
           /notes?slug=… page render must stay O(1) in garden size:
           the modal ships collapsed markup only; all searching is
           on-demand partials. Any future caching (e.g. a per-branch
           doc-index value) is optional and must be invalidated
           conservatively; premature caching is a non-goal.
    |))
   )
  )

 )
)
